caption: Core Principle
technology-rule: core-principle

Each chem grants one integrated buff package.

Every positive effect within that package:

Activates at the same time.

Has the same duration.

Uses the same delivery method.

Has the same common enhancements and limitations.

Produces the same Backlash and other shared side effects.

A chem cannot integrate effects with different durations, crashes, or activation conditions.

For example, simply mixing Psycho and Jet does not create an integrated PsychoJet. The user has taken two separate chems and receives two separate buffs. A true PsychoJet formula must be designed as a new integrated package with one common duration and modifier suite. Its final effects may differ significantly from either Psycho or Jet.

Physically mixing several chems has no special mechanical significance. Resolve each chem separately.
